IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P1-art5`

-- P1-art5-rbi: Article 5(2) to (8) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- the rules for the use of 'real-time' remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement
-- (the use point (h) of paragraph 1 lets through), authorisation, notification, national rules, reports, and the saving of other Union law.
-- The Omnibus did not change paragraphs 2 to 8 (all marked as the base text in the consolidated text); they apply from 2 February 2025 (provision group `Chapter II`).
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE the text says yes to the question the name asks; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words
-- ("only", "provided that", "shall not affect"); NOTHING not covered (before the Article applies, or the case is outside the words of the paragraph).
-- A rule answers a DEONTIC: a prohibition or a duty with a clock where the text states one (Article 5(3) 24 hours and "immediate effect", Article 5(5) 30 days),
-- otherwise a duty with no clock, which no trace can show breached (NOTES.md lists them).
-- The party is `Operator` wherever the text addresses someone the core has no constructor for (a law enforcement authority, a Member State, a market surveillance
-- authority, a data protection authority, the Commission, a judicial authority); see NEEDS-CORE.md.
-- Clocks count days: the keel's rules use the absolute day number of a date, and a rule here takes the day the clock starts as 0, so "within 24 hours" is within 1 day (fork F-5-3-24-hours).

§ `Article 5(2) to (8): the duties of the rules`

DECLARE `Art 5(2) to (8) duty` IS ONE OF
    `Art 5(2) take into account the nature of the situation and the consequences of the use`
    `Art 5(2) comply with the safeguards and conditions of the national law authorising the use`
    `Art 5(3) request the authorisation without undue delay`
    `Art 5(3) stop the use and discard and delete the data, the results and the outputs`
    `Art 5(3) take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2`
    `Art 5(4) notify the use`
    `Art 5(4) include in the notification the information specified under paragraph 6`
    `Art 5(4) include sensitive operational data in the notification`
    `Art 5(5) lay down in national law the necessary detailed rules`
    `Art 5(5) notify the national rules to the Commission`
    `Art 5(6) submit annual reports to the Commission`
    `Art 5(6) provide a template`
    `Art 5(7) publish annual reports`

§ `Article 5(2): confirming the identity, the elements, the safeguards, the authorisation conditions`

-- The words "the use of 'real-time' remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement" recur in paragraphs 2 to 6;
-- each is one BOOLEAN input here (Article 3(42), (44), (46)); the seat layer works it out from the facts of those definitions, as for P1-art5 (fork F-5-3-defined-terms).

-- src:202 | 2. The use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), shall be deployed for the purposes set out in that point only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual, and it shall take into account the following elements:
@ref Art 5(2) first subparagraph, first sentence: only to confirm the identity (src:202)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) the use satisfies the limit of being deployed only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
                AND `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2 speaks of that use "for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)"
        OTHERWISE JUST `the use is only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual`
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deployed for the purposes set out in that point only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual"

-- src:202 | 2. The use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), shall be deployed for the purposes set out in that point only to confirm the identity of the specifically targeted individual, and it shall take into account the following elements:
-- src:203 | (a) the nature of the situation giving rise to the possible use, in particular the seriousness, probability and scale of the harm that would be caused if the system were not used;
-- src:204 | (b) the consequences of the use of the system for the rights and freedoms of all persons concerned, in particular the seriousness, probability and scale of those consequences.
@ref Art 5(2) first subparagraph: take into account the elements (src:202-204)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(2) the duty to take into account the nature of the situation and the consequences of the use` MEANS
    IF     `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
       AND `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
       AND `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(2) take into account the nature of the situation and the consequences of the use`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the elements of Article 5(2), points (a) and (b), were not taken into account"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence: a trace cannot show it breached (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:205 | In addition, the use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), of this Article shall comply with necessary and proportionate safeguards and conditions in relation to the use in accordance with the national law authorising the use thereof, in particular as regards the temporal, geographic and personal limitations. The use of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be authorised only if the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment as provided for in Article 27 and has registered the system in the EU database according to Article 49. However, in duly justified cases of urgency, the use of such systems may be commenced without the registration in the EU database, provided that such registration is completed without undue delay.
@ref Art 5(2) second subparagraph: safeguards, authorisation conditions (src:205)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(2) the duty to comply with the safeguards and conditions of the national law authorising the use` MEANS
    IF     `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
       AND `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
       AND `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(2) comply with the safeguards and conditions of the national law authorising the use`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the use did not comply with the necessary and proportionate safeguards and conditions of the national law authorising it"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "shall be authorised only if the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment ... and has registered the system in the EU database":
-- a condition closed with "only if": without it, the text says no. "However, in duly justified cases of urgency, the use of such systems may be commenced without the registration
-- in the EU database, provided that such registration is completed without undue delay": a "may" gated by urgency (split site (ii), fork F-5-2-urgency): where there is no urgency the
-- base sentence's own "only if" gives JUST FALSE, so the gate failing does not leave the question unanswered.
-- src:205 | In addition, the use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), of this Article shall comply with necessary and proportionate safeguards and conditions in relation to the use in accordance with the national law authorising the use thereof, in particular as regards the temporal, geographic and personal limitations. The use of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be authorised only if the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment as provided for in Article 27 and has registered the system in the EU database according to Article 49. However, in duly justified cases of urgency, the use of such systems may be commenced without the registration in the EU database, provided that such registration is completed without undue delay.
@ref Art 5(2) second subparagraph: the use shall be authorised only if (src:205)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment as provided for in Article 27` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement authority has registered the system in the EU database according to Article 49` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a duly justified case of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration is completed without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) the use satisfies the conditions for being authorised` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT (    `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
                AND `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2 speaks of that use
        IF NOT `the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment as provided for in Article 27`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be authorised only if the law enforcement authority has completed a fundamental rights impact assessment as provided for in Article 27"
        IF `the law enforcement authority has registered the system in the EU database according to Article 49`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the case is a duly justified case of urgency` AND `the registration is completed without undue delay`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "in duly justified cases of urgency, the use of such systems may be commenced without the registration in the EU database, provided that such registration is completed without undue delay"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be authorised only if the law enforcement authority ... has registered the system in the EU database according to Article 49" (the urgency proviso needs both urgency and a registration completed without undue delay)

-- The seat's question "must I take these elements into account and comply with those safeguards?": JUST TRUE for a use of that kind for one of the objectives of point (h); NOTHING otherwise.
