@ref Art 5(2): who must take the elements into account and comply (src:202-205)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) the use must take the elements into account and comply with the safeguards and conditions of national law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF     `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
           AND `the use is for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "shall take into account the following elements" and "shall comply with necessary and proportionate safeguards and conditions"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 2 speaks of that use "for any of the objectives referred to in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)"

§ `Article 5(3): prior authorisation, urgency, rejection, the authority's conditions, no decision on the output alone`

-- "each use ... shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State
-- in which the use is to take place": the question is whether the use may begin. JUST TRUE with a prior authorisation, or in urgency with the request made without undue delay and within 24 hours;
-- JUST FALSE otherwise (the paragraph's own "shall be subject to" and "provided that"). Hours are a number: the clock of the rule below counts days (fork F-5-3-24-hours).
-- fork F-5-3-urgency (split site (ii)): the urgency sentence is a "may" gated by "in a duly justified situation of urgency"; answered JUST FALSE where there is neither an authorisation nor urgency, because the sentence before it is a flat "shall be subject to a prior authorisation"; the other reading answers NOTHING.
-- src:206 | 3. For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h) and paragraph 2, each use for the purposes of law enforcement of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, issued upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5. However, in a duly justified situation of urgency, the use of such system may be commenced without an authorisation provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours. If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted.
@ref Art 5(3) first subparagraph: prior authorisation, urgency (src:206)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prior authorisation has been granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is requested without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of hours from the start of the use to the request for the authorisation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) the use may be commenced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 3 speaks of "each use for the purposes of law enforcement of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces"
        IF `a prior authorisation has been granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF     `the situation is a duly justified situation of urgency`
           AND `the authorisation is requested without undue delay`
           AND `the number of hours from the start of the use to the request for the authorisation` AT MOST 24
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "in a duly justified situation of urgency, the use of such system may be commenced without an authorisation provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each use ... shall be subject to a prior authorisation" and "provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours"

-- The duty to request, with its clock: the clock starts when the use commences without an authorisation in a situation of urgency; the request is due within 24 hours, which this encoding
-- counts as 1 day. A request on the next day is in time; on the day after that it is late and the rule reaches BREACH.
-- src:206 | 3. For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h) and paragraph 2, each use for the purposes of law enforcement of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, issued upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5. However, in a duly justified situation of urgency, the use of such system may be commenced without an authorisation provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours. If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted.
@ref Art 5(3) first subparagraph: the request within 24 hours (src:206)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(3) the duty to request the authorisation after commencing the use in a situation of urgency` MEANS
    IF `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked` AND `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(3) request the authorisation without undue delay`
        WITHIN 1
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the authorisation was not requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted."
-- A duty introduced by "if": where the authorisation is not rejected the text imposes no such duty (JUST FALSE; a duty whose "if" is unmet, fork F-5-3-rejection-if). The time limit is "immediate": 0 days from the rejection.
-- src:206 | 3. For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h) and paragraph 2, each use for the purposes of law enforcement of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, issued upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5. However, in a duly justified situation of urgency, the use of such system may be commenced without an authorisation provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours. If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted.
@ref Art 5(3) first subparagraph: rejection (src:206)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) the use must be stopped and the data discarded and deleted` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence follows the urgency proviso and speaks of "such authorisation" requested after commencing
        OTHERWISE JUST `the authorisation is rejected`
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted"

-- src:206 | 3. For the purposes of paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h) and paragraph 2, each use for the purposes of law enforcement of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding of the Member State in which the use is to take place, issued upon a reasoned request and in accordance with the detailed rules of national law referred to in paragraph 5. However, in a duly justified situation of urgency, the use of such system may be commenced without an authorisation provided that such authorisation is requested without undue delay, at the latest within 24 hours. If such authorisation is rejected, the use shall be stopped with immediate effect and all the data, as well as the results and outputs of that use shall be immediately discarded and deleted.
@ref Art 5(3) first subparagraph: rejection, immediate effect (src:206)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is rejected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(3) the duty to stop the use and discard and delete the data` MEANS
    IF     `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`
       AND `the use commenced without an authorisation in a duly justified situation of urgency`
       AND `the authorisation is rejected`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(3) stop the use and discard and delete the data, the results and the outputs`
        WITHIN 0
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the use was not stopped with immediate effect and the data, results and outputs were not immediately discarded and deleted"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- The authority "shall grant the authorisation only where it is satisfied ... that the use ... is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h)
-- ... and, in particular, remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope": a list closed with "only where".
-- The party is the authority, an official: no seat; what it means to a deployer is that an authorisation granted without these conditions was not one the authority could grant.
-- src:207 | The competent judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding shall grant the authorisation only where it is satisfied, on the basis of objective evidence or clear indications presented to it, that the use of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system concerned is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), as identified in the request and, in particular, remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope. In deciding on the request, that authority shall take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2. No decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken based solely on the output of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system.
@ref Art 5(3) second subparagraph: the authority grants only where satisfied (src:207)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority is satisfied, on the basis of objective evidence or clear indications presented to it, that the use is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), as identified in the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) the authority may grant the authorisation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF NOT `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks of "the use of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system concerned"
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the authority is satisfied, on the basis of objective evidence or clear indications presented to it, that the use is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), as identified in the request`
                        AND `the use remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope`)
                  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall grant the authorisation only where it is satisfied"

-- "In deciding on the request, that authority shall take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2." A duty of the authority with no clock.
-- src:207 | The competent judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding shall grant the authorisation only where it is satisfied, on the basis of objective evidence or clear indications presented to it, that the use of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system concerned is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), as identified in the request and, in particular, remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope. In deciding on the request, that authority shall take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2. No decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken based solely on the output of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system.
@ref Art 5(3) second subparagraph: the authority takes into account the elements (src:207)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority is deciding on a request for an authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(3) the duty of the authority to take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2` MEANS
    IF `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked` AND `the authority is deciding on a request for an authorisation`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(3) take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the authority did not take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md, rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- "No decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system."
-- A flat negative with two elements: JUST TRUE says the decision is barred; where an element is missing the sentence does not speak to the decision (NOTHING; fork F-5-1-element).
-- src:207 | The competent judicial authority or an independent administrative authority whose decision is binding shall grant the authorisation only where it is satisfied, on the basis of objective evidence or clear indications presented to it, that the use of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system concerned is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives specified in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), as identified in the request and, in particular, remains limited to what is strictly necessary concerning the period of time as well as the geographic and personal scope. In deciding on the request, that authority shall take into account the elements referred to in paragraph 2. No decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken based solely on the output of the ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system.
@ref Art 5(3) second subparagraph: no decision on the output alone (src:207)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) the decision is barred because it produces an adverse legal effect and rests solely on the output` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Article 5 applies from 2 February 2025 (Article 113 third paragraph, point (a))
        IF `the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` AND `the decision is taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system`
        THEN JUST TRUE  -- "No decision that produces an adverse legal effect on a person may be taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a decision with both the adverse legal effect and the sole reliance on the output

§ `Article 5(4): notification of each use`

-- "each use ... shall be notified to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority in accordance with the national rules referred to in paragraph 5."
-- The time and form are national (paragraph 5): the text states no clock, so the rule has no breach path. The notification "shall not include sensitive operational data": that is a prohibition,
-- and the act of including it is a breach.
-- src:208 | 4. Without prejudice to paragraph 3, each use of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes shall be notified to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority in accordance with the national rules referred to in paragraph 5. The notification shall, as a minimum, contain the information specified under paragraph 6 and shall not include sensitive operational data.
@ref Art 5(4): notify each use (src:208)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(4) the duty to notify the use to the market surveillance authority and the data protection authority` MEANS
    IF `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked` AND `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(4) notify the use`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the use was not notified to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority"
        -- no time limit in the text (the national rules of paragraph 5 may set one): no breach path (NOTES.md)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:208 | 4. Without prejudice to paragraph 3, each use of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes shall be notified to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority in accordance with the national rules referred to in paragraph 5. The notification shall, as a minimum, contain the information specified under paragraph 6 and shall not include sensitive operational data.
@ref Art 5(4): the content of the notification (src:208)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(4) the duty to include in the notification the information specified under paragraph 6` MEANS
    IF `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked` AND `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        MUST `Art 5(4) include in the notification the information specified under paragraph 6`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the notification did not contain, as a minimum, the information specified under paragraph 6"
        -- no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md; paragraph 6 specifies no list of information for the notification itself, finding in NOTES.md)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- src:208 | 4. Without prejudice to paragraph 3, each use of a ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes shall be notified to the relevant market surveillance authority and the national data protection authority in accordance with the national rules referred to in paragraph 5. The notification shall, as a minimum, contain the information specified under paragraph 6 and shall not include sensitive operational data.
@ref Art 5(4): no sensitive operational data (src:208)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 5(2) to (8) duty`
`Art 5(4) the prohibition on including sensitive operational data in the notification` MEANS
    IF `Art 5 the Chapter II provisions apply on the date asked` `the date asked` AND `the use is of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes`
    THEN
        PARTY Operator
        SHANT `Art 5(4) include sensitive operational data in the notification`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY Operator BECAUSE "the notification included sensitive operational data"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- The seat's questions "must I notify the use?" and "may the notification include sensitive operational data?": JUST TRUE for a use of that kind; NOTHING otherwise.
